{
  "title": "The Twenty-Fifth Of Zilhajj",
  "data": "On this blessed day, [Surah al-Dahr](A80) (or al-Insan No. 76) was revealed praising the Ahl al-Bayt (a.s.) for they had observed fasting for three days and given their food to a poor, an orphan, and a captive for three days respectively. All over these three days, they used to break their fasting with water only. In view of that, the adherents (Shi’ah) of the Ahl al-Bayt (a.s.) are required to imitate their masters on these three days and give alms to the poor and the orphans, especially at the twenty-fifth night of Zilhajj, to do their best in offering food to the needy, and to observe fasting on these days. In the view of some scholars, the twenty-fifth of Zilhajj is the Day of Mubaahalah; therefore, it is proper to say [al-Ziyarah al-Jaame'ah](G13) and [Dua al-Mubaahalah](AC21), which has been previously cited."
}
